Replaced the single global `nsupdate_tsig_algorithm`/`nsupdate_tsig_key` settings with `nsupdate_tsig`, a per-nameserver mapping of TSIG keys keyed by the zone's SOA master nameserver. Dynamic DNS updates are now only sent to nameservers that have a key configured; unlisted nameservers are skipped instead of receiving an update signed with the wrong key. Also added `nsupdate_mgm_txt` to toggle the informational TXT record, and IPv6 (AAAA/PTR) and CNAME record handling, which nsupdate never supported before.
